# Dependencies dropped from every package. check() is never run, so the tools only tests need are not wanted, and they are
# what most of the dependency cycles through the hardware libraries come from (umockdev needs libgudev, libgusb, libpcap, ...).
drop umockdev
# ruby-rdoc is the makedepends of the Ruby gems that generate ri documentation, and rdoc itself needs erb, bundler and rake (gems).
drop ruby-rdoc
# Documentation toolchains: fig2dev (xfig) and dblatex (LaTeX) are only for PDF manuals, and they pull in ghostscript, gnupg and
# half of the printing stack, whose dependencies come back round to the libraries that want the manuals.
drop fig2dev
drop dblatex
# po4a translates man pages and needs the DocBook stylesheets over the network; it is a build tool for documentation only.
drop po4a
